---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site.ts';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy"
  description={`How ${site.name} handles calculator links, optional Google Analytics, cookies, fonts, email, and hosting.`}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight md:text-4xl">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-500 dark:text-ink-400">Last updated: {site.legalUpdated}.</p>

    <p class="mt-6 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      This policy describes {site.name} ({site.domain}). It covers what stays in your browser, what
      third parties may see when a page loads, and how to reach us. It is written for the site as it
      runs today. If a collection method is added later, this page will name it before or at the
      same time the code ships.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The calculator is local</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Device names, wattages, hours, duty cycles, backup days, and solar settings are processed by
      JavaScript in your browser. The calculator does not submit a form containing those values or
      save them in an account. There is no login and no
      newsletter form.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      New shareable links put the encoded device list and selected settings after #calculator? in
      the URL fragment. Browsers do not include the fragment in the HTTP page request, but anyone
      with the link can read it, and it may remain in browser history or a messaging service.
      It is not encrypted. Do not share a link if its contents are sensitive.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Older links used query parameters. Opening one sends those parameters to the host in the
      initial request. Our script moves the calculator parameters into the fragment before loading
      optional Analytics; it cannot undo that first request or earlier collection. Scripts running
      on a page can read its URL, including the fragment.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">What loads when you open a page</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      A page request reaches the host. Fonts load from Google, and Analytics loads only if you
      accept it. Legacy share URLs can include calculator inputs in the hosting request.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-8 text-base font-semibold tracking-tight">Cloudflare</h3>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      The site is served from Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare receives the IP address, browser, and URL
      of each request in order to deliver the files and to absorb abuse. Cloudflare may set a
      security cookie such as __cf_bm. That cookie is Cloudflare's, not a {site.name} login cookie.
      Incoming mail to
      <!--email_off--><a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a><!--/email_off-->
      is received through Cloudflare Email Routing and forwarded to a mailbox we monitor. There is
      no newsletter subscription associated with contacting us.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-8 text-base font-semibold tracking-tight">Google Analytics 4</h3>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Google Analytics 4 (measurement ID {site.analytics.ga4}) stays off until you choose
      "Accept analytics". After acceptance, Google's tag can collect usage, browser, device, and
      network information and set first-party cookies such as _ga. Google receives your IP address
      when handling requests; its processing rules can differ by region. We do not describe this
      as storing a truncated IP address.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Google's own description of this processing is in
      <a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>
      and
      <a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/12017362?hl=en" rel="noopener">regional data collection documentation</a>.
      We configure Analytics page location and referrer values without query strings or fragments,
      do not add calculator-input events, and disable Google signals and advertising personalization
      in the tag configuration. We have not added a Google Ads conversion tag. The calculator works
      without Analytics.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-8 text-base font-semibold tracking-tight">Google Fonts</h3>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Page text requests Fraunces, Source Sans 3, and IBM Plex Mono from fonts.googleapis.com and
      fonts.gstatic.com. Google can see the IP address of that request. Font files are not the
      calculator. If fonts are later self-hosted, this paragraph will be removed.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-8 text-base font-semibold tracking-tight">Email you send us</h3>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      If you write to {site.contactEmail}, we receive whatever you put in the message: your address,
      the subject, body, and any attachments. We use this information to handle your request and
      investigate corrections. Please do not send medical records or other sensitive information
      that is unnecessary for your question. There is no mailing list.
    </p>

    <h3 class="mt-8 text-base font-semibold tracking-tight">Affiliate cookies</h3>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      {
        site.affiliateLive
          ? 'When you follow a retailer link, that retailer or its network may set a cookie so a purchase can be attributed to this site. That cookie is theirs. The disclosure page names the programs.'
          : 'No affiliate or retailer checkout links are live. Model pages link to the manufacturer source with rel="nofollow noopener". If checkout links are added, this section and the disclosure page will name the programs on the same deploy.'
      }
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Cookies, in one list</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">
        <strong class="text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100">Google Analytics</strong> (_ga and related):
        usage measurement. Set only after you accept optional Analytics.
      </li>
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">
        <strong class="text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100">Cloudflare</strong> (for example __cf_bm):
        bot management. Set by Cloudflare on some requests.
      </li>
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">
        <strong class="text-ink-900 dark:text-ink-100">Analytics preference</strong>: the browser's
        local storage holds pss-analytics-consent for up to 180 days to remember acceptance or
        refusal. This is not an analytics identifier. If storage is unavailable, your choice may
        not persist when you leave the page. Calculator state stays in the page or a shared URL.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Use "Reject analytics" to continue without loading the tag, or "Analytics settings" in the
      footer to change your choice. Rejecting after acceptance disables the tag, removes accessible
      _ga cookies for this site, and reloads the page to stop the loaded script. It does not delete
      data previously received by Google. Blocking third-party cookies alone may not stop Analytics
      because its cookies can be first-party. Clearing site storage also clears your preference.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">How this information is used</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">To serve the pages and keep the host available.</li>
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">To see which URLs are used, so the calculator and guides can be improved.</li>
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">To answer email and to correct a wrong specification.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      We do not sell mailing lists or calculator inputs. We do not run a remarketing pixel. We do not build a
      profile of the appliances you typed.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Who else can see it</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Cloudflare (hosting and inbound mail routing), Google (optional Analytics and Fonts), and our
      email mailbox provider process information as described above. These providers may process
      information outside your country under their own terms and applicable safeguards. Information
      may also need to be disclosed to comply with a lawful request.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Retention</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      We do not maintain an account database of calculator inputs. Hosting records may include
      legacy query links; provider retention rules apply to those records. Analytics retention
      depends on the GA4 property settings and Google's policies, which can treat aggregated reports
      differently from event-level data. We do not claim a particular property retention period
      here. Contact us for the current setting. Email may be kept while a request, correction, or
      related record is needed, including legal obligations. We do not promise automatic deletion
      immediately after a reply.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Your choices</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">
        Reject optional Analytics or withdraw your choice using the footer's Analytics settings.
        You do not need to accept to use any calculator feature.
      </li>
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">
        Use Google's
        <a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Analytics opt-out add-on</a>
        if you want that control specifically.
      </li>
      <li class="max-w-[68ch]">
        Email {site.contactEmail} to ask what we still hold from a message you sent, or to ask that
        the thread be deleted.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Depending on your location and the law that applies, you may have rights to access, correct,
      delete, restrict, or receive a copy of your personal information, object to processing, or
      withdraw consent. You may also be able to complain to a data protection authority. Send
      requests to the contact address below. We may need to verify your request, and legal
      exceptions can apply. Do not send identity documents unless we explain why they are needed.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      Optional Analytics is based on your choice. Hosting and security support delivery of the
      site; email processing supports the request you send us. Where a legal basis is required,
      these activities may rely on consent, legitimate interests in operating and securing the
      site and responding to requests, or legal obligations, as applicable.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Children</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      This site is written for adults sizing backup power. It is not directed at children under 13,
      and we do not knowingly collect information from them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Changes</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      If collection changes (a new tag, a form, affiliate cookies, self-hosted fonts), this page
      gets a new "Last updated" date in the same deploy as the code. The current date is
      {site.legalUpdated}.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[68ch] text-ink-600 dark:text-ink-300">
      {site.name}, {site.domain}. Email
      <!--email_off--><a class="text-moss-700 underline dark:text-moss-300" href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a><!--/email_off-->.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
